#
# PAM configuration for synui's lock-screen fingerprint reader
# (synui-lock-fprint).
#
# pam_fprintd ALONE, deliberately. This is not the lock's auth stack — that is
# synui-lock, which includes login and runs in the other helper. This service
# exists so a swipe can be waited on in a separate process without the password
# stack behind it: if the finger does not match, the helper must FAIL, not fall
# through to a password prompt it has no password to answer.
#
# 'required' rather than 'sufficient' for the same reason. There is nothing
# after it to be sufficient over, and 'sufficient' on a lone module that fails
# leaves the stack with no successful module and PAM_AUTH_ERR anyway — but it
# reads as though a fallback exists. It does not.
#
# account is pam_permit because the real account check runs in the password
# service (synui-lock includes login, so faillock and expiry are enforced
# there); the helper calls pam_acct_mgmt against THIS service, and pam_fprintd
# supplies no account module, so an empty account stack would fail every
# successful swipe with PAM_PERM_DENIED.
#
# Missing pam_fprintd.so (the fprintd package is an optdepend, not a depend)
# makes pam_authenticate return PAM_MODULE_UNKNOWN, which the helper reports as
# "unavailable" and synui then stops asking. A machine with no reader loses
# nothing and shows nothing.
#
auth    required pam_fprintd.so
account required pam_permit.so
